From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 01:47:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] hostapd: clear reserved EHT PHY capability bits

The last octet of the EHT PHY Capabilities Information field only defines
bits 0 and 1. Clear the remaining reserved bits before advertising the
capability. Some stations reject the complete EHT capability when a driver
leaves a reserved bit set and fall back to HE operation.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11_eht.c
@@ -140,6 +140,9 @@ u8 * hostapd_eid_eht_capab(struct hostap
 	cap->mac_cap = host_to_le16(eht_cap->mac_cap);
 	os_memcpy(cap->phy_cap, eht_cap->phy_cap, EHT_PHY_CAPAB_LEN);
 
+	/* Bits 2-7 of the last EHT PHY capability octet are reserved. */
+	cap->phy_cap[EHT_PHY_CAPAB_LEN - 1] &= BIT(0) | BIT(1);
+
 	if (!is_6ghz_op_class(hapd->iconf->op_class))
 		cap->phy_cap[EHT_PHYCAP_320MHZ_IN_6GHZ_SUPPORT_IDX] &=
 			~EHT_PHYCAP_320MHZ_IN_6GHZ_SUPPORT_MASK;
